{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_project_overview", "label": "Attendance Web App README", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L1-L14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Workforce attendance, leave, scheduling and payroll for several organisations, served by one deployment across several domains: each organisation gets its own Firestore database, branding and enabled modules while sharing one codebase, Firebase project and Auth pool."}, {"id": "readme_stack", "label": "Application Stack (Next.js 16 / React 19 / Firebase)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L17-L29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_public_firebase_keys", "label": "NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_* Keys Are Not Secrets", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L49-L55", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "These keys identify the project and do not grant access - Firestore rules do the enforcing - which is why netlify.toml disables Netlify's secret scanner. Every real secret is non-NEXT_PUBLIC_."}, {"id": "readme_tenant_resolution_flow", "label": "Server-Side Tenant Resolution Flow", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L76-L97", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One build serves every domain, so the database cannot come from a build-time env var, and the browser cannot look it up either because it would need the map in order to know which database to open. The server resolves it per request and injects the answer as window.__TENANT__ before any bundle runs."}, {"id": "readme_admindbfor", "label": "adminDbFor(req) in API Routes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L96-L97", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A bare adminDb() falls back to the env default and will silently read the wrong organisation's data."}, {"id": "readme_snapshot_failsafe", "label": "Snapshot Is a Failsafe, Not a Source of Truth", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L99-L102", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Without a shipped snapshot, one bad write or one Firestore outage would leave every domain unable to resolve its own database."}, {"id": "readme_module_flags", "label": "Module Flags and Three Read Sites", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L104-L119", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "MODULE_ROUTES is read by useSidebarNav (whether the nav row renders), the (pages) layout (whether the route renders at all, so a bookmark or typed URL cannot reach a module the tenant does not have) and the page's own guard. Hiding a sidebar row on its own keeps nobody out."}, {"id": "readme_adding_a_domain", "label": "Adding a Domain Runbook", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L121-L135", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Registering the domain is the last step and the only one done in the UI. dbId is immutable once registered because re-pointing a live domain at another organisation's database is the worst thing this system could do, so there is no code path that writes one."}, {"id": "readme_platform_config", "label": "/platform Configuration Surface", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L137-L153", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Access is a separate tier from a tenant's own is_super_admin - running one organisation confers nothing here. PLATFORM_BOOTSTRAP_EMAIL is always admitted and cannot be revoked so an empty admin list can never lock everyone out; the sidebar button comes from a custom claim to cost no request while the server re-checks the real list on every call."}, {"id": "readme_test_strategy", "label": "node:test Over src/lib Pure Logic", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L59-L71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tests compile through tsconfig.test.json into .test-out/ and run on node:test with no DOM and no Firestore, so logic worth trusting belongs in src/lib rather than inside a component."}, {"id": "readme_firestore_notes", "label": "README Firestore Notes and Backups", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L181-L194", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_integrations", "label": "External Integration Surfaces", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L198-L205", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each surface has its own shared secret: FINGERPRINT_API_KEY plus a registered active device for terminals, WORKFORCE_API_KEY for the planning-app feed, ATTENDANCE_JWT_SECRET/EXTERNAL_API_KEY for the Solar app, CRON_SECRET for scheduled jobs."}, {"id": "readme_versioning", "label": "Versioning via src/data/version.json", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L208-L220", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "version.json is the single source of truth; patch bumps happen automatically on every merged PR while minor and major are manual."}, {"id": "readme_project_layout", "label": "Project Layout", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": "L157-L177", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": 